    <s:String x:Key="HelpIntroTitle">Getting started</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpIntro">Paste a YouTube, Rutube or VK Video link to a video, playlist or channel. Public content downloads without signing in. For private or restricted videos, sign in under Settings.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpDownloadTitle">Downloading</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpDownload">Use Download to watch progress, or Add to queue to run in the background. Back does not cancel a download — the job stays in the queue. Choose a folder, format, quality and file name pattern in Options.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpSourcesTitle">Sources</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpSources">YouTube, Rutube and VK Video are supported. Full YouTube quality and restricted Rutube videos use the account session saved in Settings (in-app sign-in or Firefox cookie import).</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpPlaylistsTitle">Playlists</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpPlaylists">A playlist can be saved in its own folder named after the playlist. Files are numbered in order and an .m3u file is written for sequential playback. You can scan the page for other playlists and add them to bulk download. A channel playlists catalog expands into the list of playlists.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpQueueTitle">Queue and resume</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpQueue">The Queue tab lists downloads like a torrent client. Select one or more rows with Ctrl and Shift. Pause, resume, reorder or cancel the selection. The file list shows the focused download. Right-click for the menu. On resume the app checks files already in the folder: a finished file whose duration matches the video is kept, and an incomplete .part is downloaded again. The counter is checked files out of the whole playlist.</s:String>
